# Foundation VPS: copy to .env and fill before `docker compose up --build -d`
#   cp .env.example .env
# NEVER put private keys in this file (it is read by `docker compose` and ends up in
# `docker inspect`). The bridge reserve key goes in ./secrets/reserve.key (see below).

# --- Public hostnames (DNS A records for BOTH -> this VPS public IP) ---
EXPLORER_DOMAIN=explorer.zcrypt.network
RPC_DOMAIN=rpc.zcrypt.network
# Let's Encrypt contact (use a real mailbox on a public deploy)
ACME_EMAIL=ops@zcrypt.network

# --- Build flavour ---
# Empty = PRODUCTION (no faucet, real vesting, foundation address required). Set to
# `devnet` ONLY for a local playground (enables the unbacked 0x56 faucet); a devnet image
# must never serve a value-bearing chain.
ABCI_FEATURES=

# --- Chain identity (baked into genesis at first init; all validators inherit it) ---
CHAIN_ID=zcrypt-1
# 64 hex: the foundation cold key's reward address (from the offline key ceremony,
# `cargo run -p zcrypt-core --example foundation_keys new`). Production builds refuse to
# start without it.
ZCRYPT_FOUNDATION_ADDR=
# mainnet | signet | regtest. The production image refuses regtest without a devnet build.
ZCRYPT_BTC_NET=mainnet
# mainnet: REQUIRED 160-hex-header:height (height % 2016 == 0). See mainnet-checkpoint.sh
# and verify it against a second source before launch.
ZCRYPT_BTC_CHECKPOINT=
# zBTC reserve PUBLIC key (33-byte compressed secp256k1, 66 hex, starts with 02 or 03).
# Baked into genesis as `zbtc_reserve_pk`; the node registers zBTC against it at
# InitChain, so the peg's reserve authority is fixed by genesis and can never be claimed
# by a first-come REGISTER tx. Print it with the reserve_pubkey tool (see the bridge
# watcher section below), or read it from the watcher's startup log.
ZCRYPT_RESERVE_PK=
# Foundation reserved-asset key set (64 hex, printed by `foundation_keys new` next to the
# reward address, or `foundation_keys authority <mnemonic-file>`). Baked into genesis as
# `reserved_mint_authority`. The reserved tickers (zETH, zSOL, zBNB, zTON, zDAI, zUSDT,
# zGOLD) can then be registered only by a REGISTER tx the foundation blessed offline with
# `foundation_keys bless`. Empty = the names stay parked and nobody can register them.
ZCRYPT_RESERVED_MINT_AUTH=
# Liveness sentinel (the genesis validator keeps >2/3 power until FOUNDATION_SENTINEL_DECAY
# whole ZCRYPT of external stake is bonded). false = plain BFT from block 1.
FOUNDATION_SENTINEL=true
FOUNDATION_SENTINEL_DECAY=1000000
# Browser origins allowed on the raw RPC (JSON array). Native wallets need none.
RPC_CORS_ORIGINS=[]

# --- Host ports ---
# P2P: published on the HOST so you can open it in the VPS firewall / security group.
# Validators peer to this node's external address on this port.
FOUNDATION_P2P_PORT=26656
# Raw CometBFT HTTP RPC on the host. Default is localhost-only: public wallets use
# https://$RPC_DOMAIN via Caddy (allow-listed endpoints, rate limits) instead of a raw
# 26657 on the internet.
FOUNDATION_RPC_PORT=127.0.0.1:36657

# --- State ---
# Blocks between full postcard backups of the consensus state (RocksDB is authoritative).
ZCRYPT_BACKUP_EVERY=1000

# --- Bridge watcher (only with: docker compose --profile bridge up -d) ---
# The reserve key is a Docker SECRET, not an env var:
#   umask 077; mkdir -p secrets
#   cargo run --release -p zcrypt-bridge --bin reserve_pubkey -- \
#     --wallet-seed-file <custody seed file> --write-derived-key secrets/reserve.key
# The file holds the DERIVED reserve key H("BTCBRDG", wallet seed) as 64 hex; the command
# also prints the public key to use as ZCRYPT_RESERVE_PK.
# The watcher runs as uid 10001 in its container and the secret is a bind mount, so:
#   chown 10001:10001 secrets/reserve.key && chmod 600 secrets/reserve.key
# Override the path with ZCRYPT_RESERVE_KEY_PATH if you keep it elsewhere. Keep ./secrets out of git and out of backups that leave the host.
# ZCRYPT_RESERVE_KEY_PATH=./secrets/reserve.key
# Operator bitcoind (YOUR node; the dev-profile regtest container is not part of the
# bridge profile). All three are required when the profile is enabled.
# The RPC is plain HTTP with basic auth (no TLS). Outside regtest the watcher REFUSES a
# BTC_URL that is plain http to a public address or dotted hostname: reach a remote node
# over WireGuard / VPC peering / an SSH tunnel (private IP), or front it with TLS and use
# https://. ZCRYPT_BTC_RPC_ALLOW_PUBLIC=1 overrides, at your own risk.
# BTC_URL=http://10.8.0.2:8332
# BTC_USER=
# BTC_PASS=
# BTC_NETWORK=bitcoin
# BTC_WALLET=operator
# ZCrypt blocks a redeem escrow must have left before the watcher locks BTC (default
# 475200 = 5.5 days at 1 s blocks: the 3.5-day BTC lock it funds plus a 2-day claim window).
# WATCHER_FINALIZE_MARGIN=475200

# --- Sale desk (only with: docker compose --profile sale up -d): chain/SALE-DESK.md ---
# DNS A record for this name -> this VPS; Caddy gets the certificate on its own.
SALE_DOMAIN=buy.zcrypt.network
# Satoshis per whole ZCRYPT. 0 = desk closed. Edit, then `docker compose --profile sale up -d`.
SALE_PRICE_SATS=0
# SALE_MIN_SATS=20000
# SALE_MAX_SATS=100000000
# SALE_MIN_CONF=1
# SALE_ESPLORA_URL=https://blockstream.info/api
# Dollar price shown next to the sats price in wallets: a feed (default mempool.space) or a
# fixed number. The desk SELLS in sats; the dollar figure is display only.
# SALE_BTC_USD_URL=https://mempool.space/api/v1/prices
# SALE_BTC_USD=0
# The desk's phrase is a Docker SECRET at ./secrets/sale-phrase.txt (chown 10001:10001, chmod 400).
# ZCRYPT_SALE_PHRASE_PATH=./secrets/sale-phrase.txt

# --- Dev profile (docker compose --profile dev up -d): regtest bitcoind on 127.0.0.1 ---
# BTC_USER=zcrypt
# BTC_PASS=zcrypt

# ---- Reserve-key rotation (bridge H3) ----
# The zBTC reserve key can be rotated on a running chain: generate a new key
# (`reserve_pubkey --write-derived-key ...` or any 32-byte secret), then on a host that holds
# the CURRENT key run
#   ZC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:36657 rotate_reserve --current-key-file <old.key> --new-pubkey <hex>
# New deposits must pay the new key (wallets read it from /asset/id/<id>); deposits already
# mined to the old key (plus a 6-block grace) still mint. Point the watcher's reserve_key
# secret at the NEW key and list the OLD key file(s) here (comma-separated, mounted into the
# watcher container) until everything that names them is settled:
# ZCRYPT_RESERVE_PREV_KEY_FILES=
